From 26ed8163f7df41808bdeb583646617d3c70c46b7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ayiejosh <132535860+ayiejosh@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 01:30:42 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 49/73] pco: co-issue independent ALU ops in phases 0 and 1

A main ALU instruction group has two parallel datapaths: phase 0 and
phase 1. pco_group_instrs put one op per group, so phase 1 was only ever
used by fixed multi-op mappings and float code issued at half the rate
the USC can sustain.

When a group holds a single phase 0 op, look ahead (up to 8
instructions, within the block, across register-only ALU ops) for an
independent fadd/fmul/fmad/mbyp and co-issue it in phase 1 (s3-s5 ->
ft1 -> w1). The candidate must not read or write the phase 0 dest, must
not conflict with any op it is hoisted across, and its sources must fit
the upper source encodings (commutative sources are swapped if needed).

frcp/frsq/flog/fexp are not paired: co-issuing with them gave wrong
results on BXM-4-64. A phase 1 op may overwrite a phase 0 source, as
sources are read before write-back (checked bit-exact on hardware).

PCO_DEBUG=no_dual_issue disables it.

BXM-4-64 (A733), interleaved A/B on one build, 3 rounds:
  vkheavy 2048  231.7 -> 196.4 ms/frame (1.18x), heavy FS 944 -> 786 groups
  vkrender 512    0.96 -> 0.91 ms/frame
  vkrender 2048   7.76 -> 7.38 ms/frame
Output hashes (vkheavy 256/1024, cstp/cstpf/cstpi) are bit-identical;
vkedge MSAA/helper/blend checks and vkrender pixel checks pass.
---
 src/imagination/pco/pco_debug.c        |   3 +
 src/imagination/pco/pco_group_instrs.c | 272 ++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 src/imagination/pco/pco_internal.h     |   1 +
 3 files changed, 274 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

